course: dictionary
lesson: 4570
title: Height: how tall, how high, how strong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Height is how tall something is, or how high it is above the ground. Context tells you which meaning fits. «A moving swing is heavy and fast at a child's head height» means the level of a child's head, not how tall the child is.
explain: Look at the clue words around height. A height chart, a height limit and «afraid of heights» all tell you about size or level. «The height of summer» is different: it means the strongest or busiest point of the season. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Height is a noun, and its plural is heights. «Afraid of heights» means you do not like being up high. «In height» compares how tall something is, so you can say a tree is taller in height than a bush.
fact: Height is a noun, and its plural is heights.
fact: «Height» means how tall something is, or how high it is above the ground.
fact: «The height of» something means its strongest or busiest point, as in «the height of summer».
fact: «Mount Everest» is 8,849 metres high, a height agreed by Nepal and China in 2020.
fact: On a map, contour lines join points of equal height, and lines close together mean the ground is steep.
exercise: «The height chart on the wall shows how tall Mia is.» What does height mean here? | The busiest time of the year | How loud the music is | *How tall someone is | How quickly a swing moves
exercise: «She is afraid of heights, so she will not climb the ladder.» What are heights? | Strongly sad feelings | Long, flat fields | *High places | Speedy races
exercise: «We reached the height of summer, when the park was busiest.» What does the height of summer mean? | Its coldest weeks | *Its strongest or busiest point | The first day of the holidays | A list of hot drinks
test: Sam measured the height of his plant each week. What does height mean here? | How wide the leaves are | *How tall the plant is | How much water it drinks | The colour of its flowers
test: «Stay back: a swing is heavy and fast at a child's head height.» What does head height mean? | The height of the swing seat | The top of a tree | *The level of a child's head | The depth of a pool
exam: Which phrase uses height to mean the strongest or busiest point? | Height chart | Height limit | Afraid of heights | *The height of summer
